{
  "description": "Refactor step M6, class A (docs/plans/codebase-refactor.md §6.5, K1 and K3 in §4.3): internal/api's handlers.go splits into one file per area and keeps only HandlerDeps, Handler and NewHandler, so in-flight dependency edits still apply cleanly. RegisterRoutes goes to routes.go; publish, publishOrgEvent and publishOrgEventAs to publish.go; ContentTypeMiddleware to middleware_content_type.go; Health and each area's handlers and their own helpers to <area>_handlers.go. The managed link edits of an artifact update (processManagedLinkChanges, autoVersionLinkedArtifacts, which proposal_appliers.go and the link handlers also call, linksFromPendingAdds) and the version-change summary (buildChangesSummary) go to managed_link_edits.go, which is not an area file. Three helpers more than one area file would use go to their K3 homes instead, so that the helper-home allowlist (M5) gains no entry: respondArtifactLookup (artifact and artifact-history handlers) to httperr.go, the home of the error writers; logAutoNote (the artifact copy note and the attachment figure notes) to publish.go, beside publish, as the other record a handler leaves of what it did; buildChangesList (the restore message and the update summary) to managed_link_edits.go, beside buildChangesSummary. Preview with: go run ./internal/tools/declmove -n -spec internal/tools/declmove/specs/M6.json",
  "package": "internal/api",
  "targets": [
    {
      "file": "publish.go",
      "decls": [
